WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.428 --> 00:00:11.963
Aisha Coleman: Hi Linda, hi Denise. Thanks for making time this afternoon. How's the week going over there?

2
00:00:12.995 --> 00:00:17.879
Linda Sorensen: Busy. We're two weeks from open enrollment, so the phones are already picking up.

3
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:23.253
Denise Morales: And the compliance calendar doesn't care about enrollment, so here we are.

4
00:00:23.671 --> 00:00:29.345
Aisha Coleman: Understood. Anything you want to cover first, or should I go through what I have?

5
00:00:30.632 --> 00:00:37.199
Linda Sorensen: Go ahead. I've got one thing I want to raise before we run out of time.

6
00:00:37.888 --> 00:00:47.469
Aisha Coleman: Sure. Quick numbers first: you tracked around 61,000 calls last month across the member service and lending queues. That's up about 9 percent from August.

7
00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:52.147
Linda Sorensen: That matches what I'm seeing. September was heavy on mortgage questions.

8
00:00:52.354 --> 00:00:59.996
Aisha Coleman: The Google Ads offline conversions look clean, by the way. Matched rate was 94 percent. No gaps I need to flag.

9
00:01:01.489 --> 00:01:02.934
Linda Sorensen: Good. That's been fine.

10
00:01:04.156 --> 00:01:08.814
Denise Morales: The Salesforce records are landing right too. Nobody on my team has complained.

11
00:01:09.292 --> 00:01:12.558
Aisha Coleman: How's the QM rollout going on your side?

12
00:01:13.475 --> 00:01:21.622
Denise Morales: Slow but steady. We changed the greeting scorecard item last week, and per our process it went through compliance review before we published it.

13
00:01:21.622 --> 00:01:22.640
Denise Morales: Took four days.

14
00:01:22.941 --> 00:01:27.250
Aisha Coleman: Four days sounds about like what you described in the summer.

15
00:01:27.741 --> 00:01:31.193
Denise Morales: Same process, same pace. Nobody's asking to change it.

16
00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:34.403
Aisha Coleman: Fair enough. Linda, you had something?

17
00:01:35.565 --> 00:01:53.797
Linda Sorensen: I do. It's about the renewal. I'm getting pressure from finance and procurement on how the add-ons are billed. They want to know why the QM seats, the screen pop piece, and the voice agent minutes all come as separate line items instead of one number.

18
00:01:54.331 --> 00:01:58.337
Aisha Coleman: So it's the structure of the billing, not the total?

19
00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:14.048
Linda Sorensen: Honestly, both, but the structure is what's slowing us down. Procurement has a rule that anything that arrives as a per-seat charge gets its own justification memo, and I have to write one for each.

20
00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:17.197
Aisha Coleman: How many memos are we talking about?

21
00:02:18.649 --> 00:02:35.815
Linda Sorensen: Three, and the QM one is the worst. We have nineteen part-time and seasonal agents, and most of them are on the phones maybe ten hours a week in the fall and then nearly full time in the spring.

22
00:02:35.815 --> 00:02:43.297
Linda Sorensen: Paying a full seat price for someone who works a season is the part finance keeps circling.

23
00:02:43.981 --> 00:02:46.749
Aisha Coleman: How many seats are full time right now?

24
00:02:47.566 --> 00:02:53.729
Linda Sorensen: Twenty-six. So we're paying for forty-five seats and a good chunk of them are quiet half the year.

25
00:02:54.407 --> 00:03:04.383
Denise Morales: From my side, the seasonal folks are exactly who I want scored. They're the ones who miss disclosures. So I don't want to cut them out of the program.

26
00:03:05.596 --> 00:03:16.283
Aisha Coleman: That's helpful context. I don't have an answer on the billing structure today. Can I take it back to my team and come to you with options?

27
00:03:16.853 --> 00:03:26.108
Linda Sorensen: That works. I don't need it solved this week. I need something to put in front of procurement before the budget draft in December.

28
00:03:27.504 --> 00:03:31.433
Aisha Coleman: I'll note December as the anchor. Anything else on the list?

29
00:03:32.341 --> 00:03:34.243
Linda Sorensen: No, that's my one thing.

30
00:03:35.121 --> 00:03:41.236
Aisha Coleman: Then I'll ask my team and follow up by early November so you have room before the draft.

31
00:03:42.159 --> 00:03:43.340
Linda Sorensen: Perfect. Thanks, Aisha.

32
00:03:44.473 --> 00:03:46.983
Aisha Coleman: Thanks both. Hang in there through enrollment.
